@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@
+issueNumber: MDL-89295
+notes:
+  mod_assign:
+    - message: >-
+        The `assign::grading_disabled()` method now reads the marking workflow
+        state from the user flags (`assign_user_flags`) rather than from the
+        grade record, so grades are read only in workflow states that are not
+        available to the current user. It also accepts a new optional `$marker`
+        parameter; when true, it determines whether an individual marker mark
+        (multiple marking) can be modified. Marks are read only once the overall
+        workflow state is "Ready for release" or "Released", regardless of the
+        user's capabilities. The new `assign::get_user_workflow_state()` and
+        `assign::get_mark_locked_workflow_states()` methods have been added.
+      type: changed
